  <article class="docs-content">
    <div class="eyebrow">Documentation</div>
    <h1 id="intro">Introduction</h1>
    <p>AuthKit is a complete identity platform for modern applications. This guide walks you through everything from installing the SDK to configuring SAML SSO.</p>

    <h2 id="install">Installation</h2>
    <p>Install the AuthKit Node SDK from npm. First-class SDKs are also available for Python, Go, Ruby, and .NET.</p>
    <div class="code">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="npm install @authkit/node"><svg class="" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/></svg> Copy</button>
      <pre><span class="cm"># Install the SDK</span>
npm install @authkit/node</pre>
    </div>

    <h2 id="quickstart">Quickstart</h2>
    <p>Initialize the client with your project's API key. You can find it in your <a href="/app/settings.html" class="text-primary">dashboard settings</a>.</p>
    <div class="code">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="#code-init"><svg class="" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/></svg> Copy</button>
<pre id="code-init"><span class="kw">import</span> { authkit } <span class="kw">from</span> <span class="st">"@authkit/node"</span>;

<span class="kw">const</span> auth = <span class="fn">authkit</span>({
  apiKey: process.env.<span class="num">AUTHKIT_KEY</span>,
  environment: <span class="st">"production"</span>,
});</pre>
    </div>

    <h2 id="sessions">Creating a session</h2>
    <p>Sessions represent an authenticated user. Create one after verifying credentials.</p>
    <div class="code">
      <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="#code-session"><svg class="" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/></svg> Copy</button>
<pre id="code-session"><span class="kw">const</span> session = <span class="kw">await</span> auth.sessions.<span class="fn">create</span>({
  userId: user.id,
  ipAddress: req.ip,
  userAgent: req.headers[<span class="st">"user-agent"</span>],
});</pre>
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert-info" style="margin-top:24px;">
      <svg class="" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"/></svg>
      <div><strong>Tip.</strong> Store the session token as an httpOnly cookie in production. AuthKit signs and verifies tokens automatically.</div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="webhooks">Handling webhooks</h2>
    <p>Subscribe to real-time events like <code>user.created</code>, <code>session.revoked</code>, and <code>mfa.enrolled</code>. All webhook payloads are signed with HMAC SHA-256.</p>
  </article>

